          "short": "Line through $(\\frac{3}{2},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{5}{4})$.",
          "worked": "Finding the $x$-intercept: set $y=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{4(0)}{5}&=1\\\\2x&=3\\\\x&=\\frac{3}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nFinding the $y$-intercept: set $x=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2(0)}{3}-\\frac{4y}{5}&=1\\\\-4y&=5\\\\y&=-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{align*}$$\nJoin $(\\frac{3}{2},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{5}{4})$ with a straight line.",
